---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, categories } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="About">
  <section class="page-intro shell about-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Sam Wright / Filmmaker & digital creator</p>
    <h1>
      Most things I learn
      <br />
      <em>start with a project idea.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      I work across film, digital art, software and anything else that a project may need. I enjoy the creative
      decisions and the technical problem-solving that turn an idea into
      something people can watch, explore or use.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="shell about-content">
    <div class="about-portrait" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>
        <em>Stories</em>
        <br />+ worlds
        <br />+ systems
      </span>
      <small>Sam Wright / Leeds, UK</small>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>
        A broad set of interests.
        <br />A hands-on approach.
      </h2>
      <p>
        I've enjoyed making things since I was young, from games and apps like pTable to 3D art and film.
        Most of the skills I've picked up started with something I wanted to build, 
        and my projects have a habit of growing far beyond what I originally planned.
        I enjoy exploring ideas, figuring out how things work and finding ways to bring them to life.
      </p>
      <p>
        One of my biggest influences was Interstellar. 
        It sparked my interest in space and physics, enough that I originally went to university to study Astrophysics. 
        I later realised that what fascinated me most was how the film used science to
        create believable worlds and tell human stories.
        That eventually led me towards Film, where many of my interests come together.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm now exploring those interests through filmmaking, 3D work and larger projects like my KSP short film.
        I want to create things that leave people with something, whether that's wonder, curiosity or simply wanting to see more.
        Being autistic, I sometimes find it difficult to communicate exactly what I mean, 
        but creating things gives me a way to express myself that feels much more natural.
      </p>
      <div class="about-contact">
        <a class="button button-primary" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>
          Get in touch ↗
        </a>
        {site.cv && (
          <a class="button" href={site.cv} download>
            Download CV ↓
          </a>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore the work</p>
        <h2>
          Different tools.
          <br />
          The same curiosity.
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="practice-list">
      {categories.map((category, index) => (
        <a href={`/work/?category=${category.id}`}>
          <span class="index-number">0{index + 1}</span>
          <h3>{category.label}</h3>
          <p>{category.description}</p>
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
